        "excerpt": "When gestational diabetes screening happens, how glucose challenge and tolerance tests differ, how to prepare and what results may mean.",
        "faq": [
          {
            "answer": "It depends on the test. A glucose challenge often does not require fasting; an oral glucose tolerance test usually does. Follow your appointment instructions exactly.",
            "question": "Do I need to fast for the gestational diabetes test?"
          },
          {
            "answer": "Routine screening is commonly between 24 and 28 weeks. Risk factors may lead to earlier testing and sometimes repeat testing later.",
            "question": "What week is the glucose test?"
          },
          {
            "answer": "Not always in a two-step pathway. A raised screening result usually means a diagnostic glucose tolerance test is needed.",
            "question": "Does a positive screening test mean I have diabetes?"
          }
        ],
        "featured": false,
        "heading": null,
