        "excerpt": "A practical list for labour, for after the birth and for your baby — packed by week 36, so it is one less thing to think about.",
        "faq": [
          {
            "answer": "By week 36. Around one baby in ten arrives before 37 weeks, and packing early costs nothing.",
            "question": "When should I pack my hospital bag?"
          },
          {
            "answer": "One for labour and one for after the birth is the easiest split, plus a small bag for your partner. Some hospitals limit what you can bring into the delivery room.",
            "question": "How many bags do I need?"
          },
          {
            "answer": "A long phone charger, snacks for the person supporting you, and comfortable going-home clothes for yourself.",
            "question": "What do people most often forget?"
          }
        ],
